n using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le05ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Offering Advice and Solutions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use some expressions such as \"would rather ('d rather)\" or \"might want to\" to express what someone wants or also to advice politely what to do in a particular situation."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Remember would rather + base form of a verb.<br><br> <span class=\"strong\">Correct</span>: I would rather have the vegan burger. <br><span class=\"strong\">Incorrect</span>: I would rather to have the vegan burger. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You're right. I'd rather have a free meal next time!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You might want to resolve that issue quietly."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Adverbs of Manner"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use adverbs of manner to describe how something is done.<br><span class=\"italic\">Example: She walked slowly.<br/>How did she walk? Slowly.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Many adverbs are formed by adding <span class=\"strong\">-ly</span> to an adjective:<br><span class=\"italic\">Examples: sad - sadly, curious - curiously</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You take out the letter -y and add <span class=\"strong\">-ily</span> to adjectives ending in -y.<br><span class=\"italic\">Example: angry - angrily</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The adjectives  <span class=\"strong\">fast</span>,  <span class=\"strong\">hard</span>,  <span class=\"strong\">well</span> and  <span class=\"strong\">straight</span> are exceptions.  They do not change when they become adverbs."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjective\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adverb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"nice<br/>\\t\\t\\tquiet<br/>angry<br/>harsh<br/>patient<br/>\\t\\t calm<br/>\\t\\t hard<br/>\\t\\tunusual\\t\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"nicely<br> quietly<br> angrily<br> harshly<br> patiently<br> calmly<br> hard<br> unusually\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You handled that customer nicely. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "No one was shouting angrily yesterday. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Our chef works hard to keep that impression."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "nicely"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in a pleasant manner "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You handled that customer nicely yesterday."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le05ob07aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to describe how people work at a restaurant."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "angrily"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in an angry manner "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: No one was shouting angrily yesterday!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le05ob07aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "quietly"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in a quiet manner "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'd rather resolve that issue quietly."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le05ob07aud03"}], "type": "targ